      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Put chicken, halved onion, garlic, tomatoes, green pepper, whole chilli, coriander stalks, bay leaves, cumin, and stock in a large saucepan. Bring to a gentle boil."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Reduce to a low simmer. Cook uncovered for 25 minutes until the chicken is cooked through. Skim any foam from the surface."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove the chicken and shred the meat. Strain the broth through a sieve and discard the solids. Return the broth to the pan."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "While the chicken cooks, fry tortilla strips in hot oil in a frying pan for 2 minutes per side until golden and crisp. Drain on kitchen paper."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bring broth back to a simmer. Add shredded chicken and salt. Remove from heat. Stir in lime juice."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Ladle into bowls. Top with tortilla strips and fresh coriander leaves."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Broth tastes flat",
              "cause": "The aromatics were not cooked long enough to release flavour.",
              "fix": "Add an extra squeeze of lime and a pinch of salt. If making again, let the broth simmer an extra 10 minutes before straining."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Tortilla strips go soggy fast",
              "cause": "Strips were added too early or the oil was not hot enough when frying.",
              "fix": "Fry in very hot oil and add to the soup only at the moment of serving, not before."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sopa de lima is one of the most beloved dishes of the Yucatan Peninsula in southeastern Mexico. The region has a cooking tradition distinct from the rest of the country, shaped by Mayan ingredients and centuries of isolation. The lima agria, a bitter lime local to the Yucatan, gives the soup its particular sharp edge. In Merida, the Yucatan capital, this soup appears on almost every menu. It is a light first course but satisfying enough to eat as a meal."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
